WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.300
Then the change.

2
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:04.103
The data platform book's
chapter on connection string

3
00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:07.400
migration gives it for an
application on an Arc-enabled server.

4
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.484
Integrated Security becomes Authentication
equals Active Directory Managed Identity,

5
00:00:12.484 --> 00:00:17.025
and the application's process account must
be allowed to request the host's token.

6
00:00:17.025 --> 00:00:19.148
Off Arc there's no managed identity,

7
00:00:19.148 --> 00:00:23.613
so the kit names the service-principal
mode, with a certificate preferred.

8
00:00:23.613 --> 00:00:25.313
It never suggests Default.

9
00:00:25.313 --> 00:00:27.562
The change is simple, but gated.

10
00:00:27.562 --> 00:00:30.112
Gate one: the Entra login exists.

11
00:00:30.112 --> 00:00:32.325
Gate two: the role is granted.

12
00:00:32.325 --> 00:00:36.400
Gate three: the change is tested in
a production-equivalent environment.

13
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.675
A string changed before the
gates hold fails at sign-in.

14
00:00:39.675 --> 00:00:44.210
And the scan's target is advice, not
a change: the kit rewrites nothing.
